Setting up Neon as the volunteer-call database
==============================================

Neon provides free-tier serverless PostgreSQL. The free tier includes 0.5 GB
storage, auto-suspend after 5 minutes of inactivity, and ~1s cold-start on
reconnect. This is fine for a low-traffic volunteer coordination app.

1. Create account and project
-----------------------------
- Sign up at https://neon.tech
- Create a new project (any region; us-east-2 is fine for Cloud Run us-central1)
- Create a database named "vcall" with a role/user of your choice

2. Get the connection string
----------------------------
From the Neon dashboard, copy the "pooled" connection string. It looks like:

    postgresql://vcall_user:password@ep-cool-name-123456.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/vcall?sslmode=require

For asyncpg (what the app uses), change the scheme:

    postgresql+asyncpg://vcall_user:password@ep-cool-name-123456.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/vcall?ssl=require

3. Store in GCP Secret Manager
-------------------------------
    echo -n 'postgresql+asyncpg://vcall_user:password@ep-cool-name-123456.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/vcall?ssl=require' | \
      gcloud secrets create vcall-database-url --data-file=-

To update later:

    echo -n 'new-connection-string' | \
      gcloud secrets versions add vcall-database-url --data-file=-

4. Seed the database
--------------------
Use the plain postgresql:// connection string (not asyncpg) with psql:

    export DATABASE_URL='postgresql://vcall_user:password@ep-cool-name-123456.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/vcall?sslmode=require'
    psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f scripts/initdb/01-schema.sql
    psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f scripts/initdb/02-reference-data.sql

(The local dev script `scripts/dev-db.sh` runs the same files against the
container DB; cloud seeding is the same files run via `psql`.)

5. Free tier notes
------------------
- 0.5 GB storage, 1 project, 10 branches
- Compute auto-suspends after 5 min idle; first query after suspend takes ~1s
- 191.9 compute hours/month (enough for always-on single endpoint)
- No charges; upgrade to paid if you need more storage or always-on compute
- See https://neon.tech/docs/introduction/plans for current limits

6. Upgrade path
---------------
When Neon's free tier becomes a constraint (storage, availability, cold-start
latency), see `docs/CLOUD_SQL.howto` for moving to GCP Cloud SQL. The only
runtime change is the `DATABASE_URL` secret value plus an
`--add-cloudsql-instances` flag on the Cloud Run deploy.
